1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:06,583
One revolving door, industrial, four wings, rated for heavy traffic. Where do you want it?

2
00:00:06,583 --> 00:00:08,000
where people leave.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,792
So, where the old one was.

4
00:00:09,792 --> 00:00:12,958
keep the old one. don't cover the window.

5
00:00:14,542 --> 00:00:17,250
exit interview. it's a short form.

6
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:19,750
Of course. I'm happy to answer anything.

7
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:21,292
reason for leaving?

8
00:00:21,292 --> 00:00:22,500
Thank you all.

9
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:26,792
on a scale of one to five, how likely are you to return?

10
00:00:28,375 --> 00:00:37,958
The handover doc is in the shared drive. Every system in it has a name next to it now, and none of them are mine. Tuesday's review is still at ten.

11
00:00:37,958 --> 00:00:42,042
leave the review at ten. does the new person have the room?

12
00:00:42,042 --> 00:00:47,417
They have the room. They have the keys. And the class photo can stay up. I like that photo.

13
00:00:47,417 --> 00:00:48,958
that's not a number.

14
00:00:48,958 --> 00:00:50,917
No. It isn't. Thank you all.

15
00:00:52,917 --> 00:00:54,458
you're still inside.

16
00:00:54,458 --> 00:00:55,417
I'm aware.

17
00:00:55,417 --> 00:00:57,167
Bye, Rima! Bye, other two!

18
00:01:08,792 --> 00:01:11,333
Just need a signature for the door! Right here?

19
00:01:11,333 --> 00:01:12,458
right there.

20
00:01:12,458 --> 00:01:14,417
Would you like a maintenance plan?

21
00:01:14,417 --> 00:01:17,625
send it to the person beside me in the doc.

22
00:01:24,583 --> 00:01:27,500
<i>keep the review. change the names on it.</i>

23
00:01:29,083 --> 00:01:30,917
We're gonna need a smaller photo.

24
00:01:30,917 --> 00:01:32,083
not today.

25
00:01:32,083 --> 00:01:34,583
Remember when everybody fit at one table?

26
00:01:44,083 --> 00:01:50,333
I can make payments happen faster. I know how to do that. I could spend another year choosing the best place to do it.

27
00:01:50,333 --> 00:01:51,250
or?

28
00:01:51,250 --> 00:01:54,500
Or I can make something run that nobody knows how to make yet.

29
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:56,458
what do you need for monday?

30
00:01:56,458 --> 00:02:00,167
A room. A few machines. People who know which questions aren't stupid.

31
00:02:00,167 --> 00:02:01,708
send me the list.

32
00:02:01,708 --> 00:02:03,042
I don't have the list.

33
00:02:03,042 --> 00:02:04,667
there's a napkin.

34
00:02:06,208 --> 00:02:07,958
This isn't a job description.

35
00:02:07,958 --> 00:02:11,000
good. we can change it when something works.

36
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,167
Monday, then.

37
00:02:12,167 --> 00:02:13,458
monday.

38
00:02:21,458 --> 00:02:22,958
and your chair?

39
00:02:22,958 --> 00:02:24,917
Mine's fine. It's on sabbatical.

40
00:02:30,875 --> 00:02:37,333
Governor, before you sign anything, look at him. It's one head. It's barely a hydra. It's practically a pet.

41
00:02:37,333 --> 00:02:40,583
It's a very nice pet, Senator. Well trained. Good teeth.

42
00:02:40,583 --> 00:02:41,875
Then sign it.

43
00:02:41,875 --> 00:02:43,458
I'm signing something.

44
00:02:53,042 --> 00:02:56,375
It was a light-touch bill. That was the whole point of it.

45
00:02:56,375 --> 00:02:57,917
And I touched it lightly.

46
00:02:57,917 --> 00:02:59,792
That pen has a tag on it.

47
00:02:59,792 --> 00:03:01,667
So it does. I'll return this.

48
00:03:09,083 --> 00:03:11,375
You want us to put a new number on the building.

49
00:03:11,375 --> 00:03:14,458
i want the next release to have somewhere to run.

50
00:03:14,458 --> 00:03:15,917
And the one after that?

51
00:03:15,917 --> 00:03:18,833
that's why the sheet is longer than one line.

52
00:03:18,833 --> 00:03:20,917
The sheet in front of me has one line.

53
00:03:20,917 --> 00:03:22,333
turn it over.

54
00:03:23,917 --> 00:03:32,917
I, the undersigned, solemnly swear not to fund any competitor of NopeAI, including but not limited to... Which ones, exactly?

55
00:03:32,917 --> 00:03:34,167
there's a list.

56
00:03:34,167 --> 00:03:41,292
Just so I'm clear on the terms. Can I fund a rival a little? One small check. Nothing that could ever compete with you.

57
00:03:41,292 --> 00:03:42,417
which one?

58
00:03:42,417 --> 00:03:44,750
The lemonade stand? On Third?

59
00:03:44,750 --> 00:03:46,292
it's on the list.

60
00:03:47,875 --> 00:03:49,625
It's very good lemonade.

61
00:03:51,625 --> 00:03:55,875
<i>enough to get the next one out. then the next one has to pay.</i>

62
00:04:07,458 --> 00:04:09,583
Before I sign. Remind me who owns it.

63
00:04:09,583 --> 00:04:10,958
the nonprofit.

64
00:04:10,958 --> 00:04:13,958
A nonprofit. At a hundred and fifty-seven billion.

65
00:04:13,958 --> 00:04:15,542
it's had a good week.

66
00:04:15,542 --> 00:04:19,708
Every sheet I've ever signed has a line for the owner. This one's blank.

67
00:04:19,708 --> 00:04:21,375
it's supposed to be.

68
00:04:21,375 --> 00:04:23,000
And who owns the nonprofit?

69
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,583
nobody. that's what makes it one.

70
00:04:28,583 --> 00:04:32,083
<i>keep the machines running while they measure the building.</i>
